※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7025 LANG_MACRO_ANSWERS_OTHERWISE

※ What replaces the invocation is a piece of the program, so that is what a macro
※ answers.  One that worked a number out puts it into a tree with `$(…)`, which is
※ what says where in the program the number goes.

macro counted(e: syntax) → u8:
    1u8

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
